unbalan+ 2081343 2081341 2081343  0    1 14:59 ?        00:00:00 timeout 18000 systemd-run --user --scope -q -p TasksMax=1024 -p MemoryMax=24G -- timeout 17000 kimi -p # Brief: make the LCB adapter and the LLVM printer linear (ISS-0030) — branch lcb-numbering  You work in the full clone /home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-lcb-numbering, branch `lcb-numbering`, based on main ea212942 (slice 0 landed). Its first commit (4eabaffa) files ISS-0030 in ISSUES.tsv; read that row first — it has the measurements, the reproducer and the cause. Then read AGENTS.md (repository root), CLAUDE.md, Concrete/README.md (pipeline, "The `adapter_correct` proof, in layers", gates), Concrete/Backend/LCB.lean and Concrete/Backend/LLVM.lean.  Do NOT push, do NOT touch git remotes, do NOT run `git rebase/reset/clean/stash`. Commit on the branch in small commits ("ISS-0030: ..."). Every command bounded with `timeout`. You may run `timeout 3600 lake build Concrete` (this is a proof-heavy build; run it at most a few times, and never two builds at once). Never run the native gates (scripts/checks/compiler/*.sh); I run them on the CI server. Scratch only under mktemp.  ## The defect (confirmed by Codex from source)  - Concrete/Backend/LCB.lean: `regId p r := (ids p).lookup r` (line ~103) rebuilds `ids p` (lines   ~75-79, which computes `blockBase p j` and `instBase b i`, prefix sums, per entry: Θ(n²)) on every   operand lookup, so `adapt` and `emit` are Θ(n³). `numberingOk` (~95-99) adds quadratic List.Nodup   and membership checks; `adaptInst` repeats prefix sums; `adaptPhi` scans every block for incoming   edges per phi (`incoming`). - Concrete/Backend/LLVM.lean: `print` (~87-90) calls `phis p j b` per block, which rebuilds `edges p`   (~57-62) and filters it for target j: Θ(n²). - Measured: LCB.emit 27.9 ms at k=10 and 21.6 s at k=100 (exponent 2.89); LLVM.module exponent 1.52. - Structural cause: closed specification functions (numbering and predecessor relations as   functions of position, chosen for the proofs) also serve directly as executable queries.  ## The fix (decided; do not change the approach)  Keep the existing definitions and every existing theorem as the REFERENCE. Add a prepared representation computed once per program and prove it equal to the reference, so that `Proof.adapter_correct`, `Proof.emit_correct`, `Proof.artifact_correct`, `Proof.artifact_of_emit_error` and every other theorem keep their EXACT statements (same names, same hypotheses, same conclusions):  1. Numbering: build the id table once with running block/instruction offsets (a single pass), and    a lookup structure (e.g. `Std.HashMap Reg Nat` or an array indexed by register when registers are    dense — choose what you can prove cleanly in core Lean; no Mathlib) whose lookup is proved equal    to `regId p r` for every `r`, including the malformed-input cases `adapt` refuses (first    definition wins, exactly as `List.lookup`). Prove the generated list equals `ids p` and the    offsets equal `blockBase`/`instBase`. 2. Validation: replace `numberingOk`'s quadratic checks in the executable path with an equivalent    linear (or n log n) check proved to return the same Bool as `numberingOk p`, so acceptance and    refusal are unchanged. 3. Incoming edges: group edges by target once (preserving predecessor order and both conditional    arms, exactly the order `incoming p j` gives), proved equal to `incoming p j` for every j. Use it    in the LCB adapter's phis and in the LLVM printer's phis (`LLVM.phis`), proved equal to the    current printed text (the printer is unverified, P_print, but its output must not change: prove    `printFast b = print b`, or at least the module text equality, so gate outputs stay byte-identical    and the trusted-base golden and repro manifests are unchanged). 4. Define the fast functions (`adaptFast`/`emitFast` or replace the bodies of `adapt`/`emit` with    the fast code), prove `adaptFast p = adapt p` (and the emit equality), and make the executable    entry points (`LCB.emit`, `LLVM.module`, whatever slice0_bir.lean and the gates call) use the    fast code. If you replace the bodies, the reference definitions keep existing under a clear name    (e.g. `adaptSpec`) and the proofs are re-pointed by rewriting with the equality — the theorem    statements visible in the golden (tests/golden/slice0_trusted_base.txt) must not change; if any    statement must change, stop and say why instead. 5. Axioms: only propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound; no sorry, no native_decide, no partial,    unsafe, implemented_by, extern or opaque (the trust ban and gate 9 check this). 6. Evidence: measure with the reproducer (`lake env lean --run` a copy of    scripts/checks/compiler/scaling.lean... it is on another branch: instead write a small probe under    mktemp that times LLVM.module and LCB.emit on a scaled family of k = 1, 10, 100, 1000 blocks with    a linear structural digest) before and after; report the numbers and exponents in your final    message and in a changelog.d fragment. Target: exponent ≤ 1.2 for both at 10→100 and 100→1000. 7. Add the ISS-0030 closure evidence to nothing yet (I close the issue after the server gates).  ## Constraints  - No language/spec decisions; ConcreteSpec/ untouched. - Update Concrete/README.md where it describes the numbering (layer 3) only if the design text   becomes wrong; keep its style. - Final message: commits, build result (warnings are errors), axioms of the headline theorems   (unchanged), before/after timings, open questions.
