unbalan+ 2272826 2272824 2272826  0    1 15:06 ?        00:00:00 timeout 14400 systemd-run --user --scope -q -p TasksMax=1024 -p MemoryMax=24G -- timeout 13000 kimi -S session_5ca3ac88-b0e8-4aaf-8351-53a7465cfdeb -p Review round 1 of branch trusted-base. It is now REBASED: HEAD is 5e91dc13, on top of gates-manifest c2245c99 (main ea212942 + the test manifest). Run `git log --oneline -6` first. Same rules as before (no push, no remotes, no rebase/reset/clean/stash, bounded commands). NEW: you may run gate 9 to verify fixes, one run at a time, under nice:   `timeout 3000 nix develop --command nice -n 10 bash scripts/checks/compiler/slice0_trusted_base.sh` If the LCB build fails there with "failed to create thread", run it on a machine with fewer limits... you can't; then say so and I will run it on the CI server. Commit fixes as commits whose messages say "review round 1".  CI-server result at 5e91dc13 (concrete-ci-2): the golden, both README tables and the full-library audit ("trusted declarations: 0") pass. Then:   FAIL unlisted trusted declaration Concrete.Control.f [extern, opaque]   FAIL control: the trusted-code audit did not reject the extern for the planted reason The audit DID reject it; the control read the wrong file (Codex finding 1). The tool trace and the other controls did not run after that.  Findings to fix (Codex): 1. (P1) Negative controls make gate 9 fail unconditionally. print_lean returns before writing the .out file, so the extern and library-axiom controls grep a file that doesn't exist. Inspect the bounded .raw/.err output on failure, or keep the capped output before returning the failure status, and make sure a missing file can't abort the script under set -e. 2. (P1) strace's unfinished/resumed execve records are dropped: `execve(...) <unfinished ...>` followed by `<... execve resumed>) = 0` match neither pattern, so an unlisted child can run unseen. Reconstruct unfinished/resumed calls by PID, or use `-ff -o prefix` per-process traces. Add a parser control: a recorded trace containing a successful split execve of an unlisted program must fail, naming it. Keep ignoring failed PATH-lookup attempts (= -1 ENOENT). 3. (P1) The build runs outside the tool trace. slice0_common.sh's `lake build Concrete lean-compiler-backend/lcb` runs before tracing starts, so a new Lake build hook invoking an unlisted tool escapes. Trace the build too: run a `lake build` under strace in the gate (the incremental build after the shared one is cheap), and list Lake's legitimate children (git, lean, leanc/clang for the lcb exe, ar, ...) as part of the Lake/Lean components. A fresh build is the daily tier's job; say so in the header. 4. (P2) The axiom audit only sees modules imported by `Concrete`. Add a population check: every .lean file
 under Concrete/ is in the import closure of Concrete.lean, and an unimported module fails, with a control. `example`s are discarded by Lean before the audit: either audit examples the way scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh's leg X does for the spec (read it; reuse its lean_lex.py approach rather than writing a second one), or state that examples carry no trust because they are discarded, and refuse native_decide/ofReduceBool in examples lexically. Prefer reusing leg X's mechanism. Add a control: an example proved by `decide +native` must fail. 5. (P2) The `_unsafe_rec` exemption hides ordinary declarations. Exempt a twin only when it is the compiler-generated twin of a `partial` definition (check the parent's `implemented_by`/partial relationship as Lean records it), and always check extern and implemented_by attributes on it. Add a control with a hand-written `Concrete.Control.f._unsafe_rec`. 6. (P2) Enforce "exactly once": reject duplicate component ids, require each audited name (tool, declaration, axiom) to be owned by exactly one component, and require a trusted declaration to belong to a trusted component (not to `.notTrusted`). Add one control per rule.  When the gate runs end to end, report the exact set of exec'd programs it observed for the build, the emitter and the native build. Final message: commits, run summary, anything not fixed with a reason.
