unbalan+ 2529889 2529842 2529889  0    1 15:14 ?        00:00:00 /nix/store/g89cgp8457qywnzr3675d83s4haxgv34-python3-3.13.12-env/bin/python3 -I /home/unbalancedparen/projects/clones/wip-signoff-hardening/scripts/checks/lib/bounded_exec.py --timeout 14400 --kill-after 10 --status /tmp/bounded.ScY4IH/run.0CagiJ/status -- kimi -p You are the writer for branch wip/signoff-hardening of the Concrete repo, in this clone (~/projects/clones/wip-signoff-hardening), from main f7a973b0. scripts/land/signoff.sh (owner sign-off records, R-0618) and the pre-push hook's notes tier have five confirmed bugs, and two owner decisions add rules. Fix, control and file all of them. Read scripts/land/signoff.sh's header first: it is the contract.  Codex's reproducers are saved at .git/g-repro.sh (G1-G3) and .git/f-repro.sh (F3, F4 are the parts on signoff.sh; ignore its other parts). Run reproducers only bounded (source scripts/checks/lib/bounded.sh; bounded_run 60 -- ...), in temporary repositories with no hooks, no network, never pushing anywhere.  BUGS (all Codex-CONFIRMED at main f7a973b0 / ea212942): - ISS-0023 (high), G1: signoff.sh:75 (used for the quote at :159) resolves the quote's hex prefix with ref-aware `git rev-parse`, so a branch named like an ambiguous prefix selects one object: two commits sharing 6efc0de, `git branch 6efc0de <a>` makes `record` accept quote "approve 6efc0de" for a. Structural cause: object-prefix validation uses ref-aware resolution. Fix: resolve prefixes only against objects (e.g. `git rev-parse --disambiguate=<prefix>` or `git cat-file --batch-check` on the object store, refusing ambiguity), never refs; the same for every prefix check in signoff.sh (request bodies too). - ISS-0024 (medium), G2: .githooks/pre-push:54-57 recognises an owner-signoff push by topology, filenames and modes only: a parentless commit of seven 100644 files each containing `x` passes the no-source-tree tier (exit 0). The positive control at scripts/checks/review_tool.sh:311-320 pins this loophole. Structural cause: the hook does not validate contents or bind them to the ref's subject SHA. Fix: the hook runs `signoff.sh verify <sha from the ref name>` semantics on the pushed commit (with an explicit base the record allows the hook to determine, or a structural verify mode that checks everything except the cap's base-dependent part — choose and justify), and refuses anything that does not verify; fix the control to expect refusal of junk and acceptance of a real record. - ISS-0025 (low), G3: signoff.sh:140-143 (reached by verify at :219, used by train.sh:522) does not check the record commit is parentless: a valid tree re-committed with the source commit as parent verifies. Fix: verify requires zero parents. - ISS-0026 (high), F3: signoff.sh:194 (header inserted at :113) treats any occurrence of the SHA in the request body as targeting: a request "Review exact commit B. Do not review C; that is a later unreviewed change." signs C, because record prepends `reviewed: C` itself. Structural cause: incidental SHA mention counts as targeting, and the binding header is generated by the recorder. Fix: the binding must come from the request as sent — the request file must itself begin with `reviewed: <full sha>` (or an equivalently structured line the reviewer was actually sent), record must not synthesise it, and the body must not name any other commit as the one under review; choose the smallest rule that makes the reproducer fail and keep existing recorded refs verifiable (check refs/owner-signoff/ea5181b5… and refs/owner-signoff/fb097fa4… still verify, fetching them from origin read-only; if a rule would invalidate them, stop and report instead of loosening). - ISS-0027 (medium), F4: signoff.sh:202 filters for ACCEPT|REJECT before taking the last VERDICT line, so "VERDICT: ACCEPT" followed by "VERDICT: BLOCKED" records as accepted. Fix: take the last `VERDICT:` line of any value first, then require it to be ACCEPT or REJECT.  OWNER RULES (owner decisions 2026-11-08, "all yes"): - R1, item 1, writer substitution: when a model wrote the branch, that model never reviews it. record/verify take the writer's model from the record (new key, e.g. `writer: codex|kimi|agy|claude`) WITH evidence (a `writer-evidence:` value naming the commit authors/trailers or a writer-log file included in the record with its sha256). The writer can never be a reviewer. The required reviewer set is {codex, kimi, agy} minus the writer, and each remaining reviewer must ACCEPT with full repository access (its output must contain `REPOSITORY: readable` and name files it read; a REPOSITORY: unreadable or missing line is refused). The record states who wrote 
the branch and why that model's review is absent (e.g. `absent-<model>: writer`). When the writer is not one of the three (claude), the current three-reviewer rule stands. Keep existing records (no writer key) verifying under the current rule; document that. - R2, rounds for manually reviewed branches: when reviews ran outside review.sh, rounds-at may point at a recorded review-evidence commit instead of a review.sh note. Define it: a ref (e.g. refs/review-evidence/<full sha of the reviewed commit>) to a parentless commit whose tree holds, per round and reviewer, the exact request, the raw output, a manifest with each file's sha256, the reviewed SHA, and `repository: readable`. The cap check counts its rounds. A diff-only review (no `repository: readable`, or a failure text) is never counted as clean. Provide `signoff.sh evidence ...` (or a separate small script in scripts/land/) to build and verify such commits locally (push nothing); the hook tier accepts refs/review-evidence/* only when it verifies (same treatment as ISS-0024).  CONTROLS (scripts/checks/landing_script.sh and/or scripts/checks/review_tool.sh, wherever the existing sign-off controls live), one per bug reproducer (each fails on main's signoff.sh and passes after), plus for the rules: a writer listed as reviewer is refused; a missing non-writer ACCEPT is refused; a diff-only review is refused; a valid substituted set records and verifies; a review-evidence commit with readable rounds counts toward the cap and one without `repository: readable` does not.  FILING: ISSUES.tsv rows ISS-0023..ISS-0027 in the file's columns (date 2026-11-08, area ci, evidence with the reproducer facts above and "Codex confirmed 2026-11-08 at main f7a973b0" (G1-G3) / "at main ea212942" (F3, F4), found by full-access verification of fb097fa4 and the retroactive review of b7f30d36; owner R-0618; severities as above; closure_condition naming the controls; status closed by this fix). Run scripts/checks/issues.sh. Update signoff.sh's header contract, docs/LANDING.md and docs/REVIEW.md where they describe sign-offs; do not edit docs/decisions.md or ROADMAP.md. Add changelog.d/2026-11-08-signoff-hardening.md citing ISS-0023..0027 and owner items 1 and the rounds rule.  Run inside `nix develop .#gates`: bash scripts/checks/landing_script.sh, bash scripts/checks/review_tool.sh, scripts/checks/issues.sh, bounded. Commit on wip/signoff-hardening in logical commits (do not push). If any rule needs a decision you cannot take from the text above, stop and report it rather than choose. End with a short report: files changed, the record format changes, controls and results, checks run, anything left open.
