 and helpers) into ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Surface0.lean (imported by ConcreteSpec.lean), so the spec proof gates (axioms.sh, trust_ban.sh, kernel_replay.sh, external.sh) cover them; keep implementation-correspondence theorems with the implementation. 3. Errors: prove the error results, including the first-error offset (the offset is the first byte at which no well-formed continuation exists — state it declaratively and prove the decoder returns exactly it), fix the mislabelled error (a non-continuation byte where a continuation is required is not `.unexpectedContinuation`; distinguish a missing/invalid continuation from a lone continuation byte), and stop at the first error: factor one total single-scalar step, iterate it so decoding and the NUL/BOM source check short-circuit at the first error (no whole-file evaluation before reporting), structurally recursive or tail-recursive. 4. Trust gates: bring Concrete/ under scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh (no exemption for Lex.lean or anything else), register Concrete.Lex's soundness/completeness/error theorems in Concrete/Premises.lean and tests/golden/slice0_trusted_base.txt (and the axiom golden as the gates require). Remove both `set_option maxRecDepth` options by restructuring the proofs so they do not need them (e.g. decidable instances via a boolean checker with an iff lemma, or lemmas that scale with input length) — proof structure that scales is the point; do not add a trust_ban exemption. 5. agy's medium items: drop the redundant hypothesis in checkSource_complete, add the packaged iff forms (decode_ok_iff, lineComment_some_iff) and the negative lemma (decode error -> no decoding), and model comment skipping without building a discarded list. 6. Surface0's module header gets the standard PROPOSED header used by every ConcreteSpec/Spec module, and each declaration's doc comment cites the decision row it encodes.  OWNER RULE (2026-11-08, verbatim: "ALWAYS tell the reviewrs to do the best long term thing rather than cuitting corners"): judge and fix by the best long-term design. Never cut corners for speed, a smaller diff or fewer rounds. As a reviewer, report any shortcut, containment patch or corner cut as a real finding and say what the long-term fix is. As a writer, implement the structural fix, not a containment patch; if staging is truly unavoidable, record the long-term design and name its roadmap row.  The branches wip/slice0-lexer-ws (e474d8f0) and wip/slice0-lexer-tokens (da687c9e), written by Kimi, stack on this one and will rebase afterwards: keep public names stable where the fix allows, and list every rename in your report. Run inside the repository's nix devshell, bounded: lake build of the touched targets, bash scripts/proofs/axioms.sh (or the axiom check the repo uses), bash scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh, the trusted-base gate scripts/checks/compiler/slice0_trusted_base.sh, and bash scripts/checks/run.sh if it is cheap (say if not). No full suites beyond that. Do not edit docs/decisions.md or ROADMAP.md. Extend changelog.d/2026-11-08-lexer-utf8.md. Commit in logical commits. End with a short report: what changed per finding, theorem list, renames, gates run and results, anything left open.  agy's findings (verbatim): #### 1. [HIGH] Undecided lexical rules encoded in `Surface0` and `Concrete.Lex` (source-wide NUL/BOM pre-refusal and bare-`CR` line-comment termination) - **Locations**:   - [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:4-5](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L4-L5), [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:56-59](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L56-L59), [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:70-82](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L70-L82), [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:122-123](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L122-L123)   - [Concrete/Lex.lean:18-26](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L18-L26), [Concrete/Lex.lean:182-187](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L182-L187), [Concrete/Lex.lean:345-351](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L345-L351), [Concrete/Lex.lean:424-429](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L424-L429), [Concrete/Lex.lean:435](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L435) - **Problem**:   1. `SourceOk` (`∃ cs, Utf8.Decodes bs cs ∧ ∀ c ∈ cs, c ≠ 0 ∧ c ≠ 0xFEFF`) encodes a source-wide ban on `U+0000` and `U+FEFF` at every position in the file prior to lexing, and classifies any `U+FEFF` anywhere in the file (even at byte offset `> 0`, e.g. [Concrete/Lex.lean:427](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L427)) as `.bom`. `SYN-5@3` ([docs/decisions.md:1076-1078](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/docs/decisions.md#L1076-L1078)) states only that *"A source file is UTF-8 text"*; no owner decision establishes a pre-lexing `U+0000`/`U+FEFF` filter over the whole file (which would also ban `U+FEFF` inside comments and string literals).   2. `LineEnd c := c = 10 ∨ c = 13` makes bare `CR` (`13`) end a `//` line comment. Neither `SYN-6@3` nor any owner decision approves bare `CR` as a line terminator; the frozen compiler ended `//` comments only at `LF` (`10`) or EOF ([legacy/Concrete/Frontend/Lexer.lean:90-95](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/legacy/Concrete/Frontend/Lexer.lean#L90-L95)). Allowing bare `CR` to terminate a `//` comment lets code hidden after `\r` on the same `\n`-delimited line execute. - **Long-term fix**:   Remove undecided character/line-ending rules from `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` and `Concrete/Lex.lean`. If a specific policy on leading UTF-8 BOM, control characters (`NUL`, bare `CR`), and line endings is desired for `Surface0`, present the options and a recommendation (e.g., `LF` / `CRLF` line endings only, refusing bare `CR` outside string escapes, and handling non-token characters in the token grammar) to the owner first and record the owner's dated answer in `docs/decisions.md` before encoding it in `ConcreteSpec`. #### 2. [HIGH] Duplicate UTF-8 specification in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/` and specification theorems placed in the compiler (`Concrete/Lex.lean`) instead of `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/` - **Locations**:   - [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:11-53](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L11-L53) vs. [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Borrow.lean:513-539](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Borrow.lean#L513-L539)   - [Concrete/Lex.lean:105-120](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L105-L120) (`encodes_scalar`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:168-180](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L168-L180) (`decodes_unique`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:377-382](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L377-L382) (`lineComment_unique`)   - [ConcreteSpec.lean:1-7](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec.lean#L1-L7) - **Problem**:   1. `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Borrow.lean` already defines UTF-8 scalar well-formedness (`ConcreteSpec.Borrow.isScalar`, `ConcreteSpec.Borrow.Utf8`), with `utf8_split` and `text_view_utf8` proved in `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Borrow.lean`. `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` introduces a second, unconnected UTF-8 definition (`ConcreteSpec.Surface0.Utf8`), violating P2 ("one authoritative definition") and R-0560/R-0571.   2. Pure specification theorems about `ConcreteSpec.Surface0` (`encodes_scalar`, `decodes_unique`, `encodes_step_unique`, `encodes_determ`, `lineComment_unique`) are placed in `Concrete/Lex.lean` instead of `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Surface0.lean` (cf. [Concrete/README.md:161](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L161)). As a result, `scripts/spec/lean_site.sh` displays `0` theorems for `Surface0` in the owner view, and none of the four proof-integrity gates (`axioms.sh`, `trust_ban.sh`, `kernel_replay.sh`, `external.sh`) check these theorems. - **Long-term fix**:   Unify the UTF-8 definition in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/` so source decoding and `Text`/`Borrow` share one authoritative UTF-8 specification, move the specification-level theorems (`encodes_scalar`, `decodes_unique`, `lineComment_unique`, and their helper lemmas) into `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Surface0.lean`, and import `ConcreteSpec.Proofs.Surface0` in `ConcreteSpec.lean` (updating `scripts/proofs/axioms.golden` accordingly). #### 3. [HIGH] Unproved error reporting, non-short-circuiting non-tail recursion in `decodeAt`/`sourceAt`, and deferred first-error-offset TODO - **Locations**:   - [Concrete/Lex.lean:31-51](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L31-L51) (`badSequence`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:58-80](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L58-L80) (`decodeAt`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:182-212](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L182-L212) (`sourcePrepend`, `sourceAt`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:348-351](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L348-L351) (`scanLine`)   - [changelog.d/2026-11-08-lexer-utf8.md:5-6](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/changelog.d/2026-11-08-lexer-utf8.md#L5-L6) - **Problem**:   1. `sourcePrepend` ([Concrete/Lex.lean:182-187](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L182-L187)) states `/-- Refuse NUL or BOM before inspecting the remaining source. -/`, and is called as `sourcePrepend off a.toNat (sourceAt (off + 1) bs)`. Because Lean 4 is call-by-value, `sourceAt (off + 1) bs` is evaluated across the entire remainder of the file *before* `sourcePrepend` executes.   2. Both `decodeAt` and `sourceAt` duplicate the 4-way match, recurse in non-tail position (`prepend ... (decodeAt ...)`), and inspect up to 4 bytes `[a, b, c, d]` before calling `badSequence` even when `a` is a 1-, 2-, or 3-byte lead that already failed at `a` or `b`. Similarly, `scanLine` ([Concrete/Lex.lean:348-351](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L348-L351)) is non-tail-recursive.   3. `badSequence` ([Concrete/Lex.lean:43](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L43)) labels a non-continuation byte (`b < 0x80 ∨ b > 0xBF`, such as ASCII `0x41` after `0xC2` in [Concrete/Lex.lean:412](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L412)) as `.unexpectedContinuation` even when `b` is not a continuation byte.   4. No theorem connects `.error e` to the specification; the first-error-offset theorem was deferred as a TODO in `changelog.d/2026-11-08-lexer-utf8.md:5-6`. Under the 2026-11-08 owner rule (never cut corners; implement the best long-term design), shipping an unproved `badSequence` sidecar and deferring the error theorem is a shortcut. - **Long-term fix**:   Factor single-scalar decoding into one total step function `decodeStep (off : Nat) (bs : List UInt8) : Except DecodeError (Nat × Nat × List UInt8)` that dispatches on the lead byte's length class and fails immediately at the first offending byte, iterate it tail-recursively so execution short-circuits on the first error in $O(1)$ stack space, distinguish a missing continuation byte from a lone continuation byte, and prove the first-error-offset soundness theorem now rather than leaving a TODO. #### 4. [HIGH] `Concrete/Lex.lean` is completely outside the proof-integrity and trusted-base gates, and relies on `set_option maxRecDepth` - **Locations**:   - [Concrete/Lex.lean:13](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L13) (`set_option maxRecDepth 2048`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:402](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L402) (`set_option maxRecDepth 100000`)   - [Concrete/Premises.lean:64-72](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Premises.lean#L64-L72)   - [tests/golden/slice0_trusted_base.txt:10-16](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/tests/golden/slice0_trusted_base.txt#L10-L16)   - [scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh:42-50](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh#L42-L50) - **Problem**:   1. `scripts/proofs/*` checks only `ConcreteSpec`, and `scripts/checks/compiler/slice0_trusted_base.sh` checks only the theorem names listed in `Concrete.Premises.theorems` ([Concrete/Premises.lean:64-72](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Premises.lean#L64-L72)). Because `Concrete.Lex`'s theorems are not registered in `Concrete.Premises.theorems` and `trust_ban.sh` does not scan `Concrete/`, a `sorry`, `native_decide`, or extra axiom in `Concrete/Lex.lean` would pass every gate.   2. `Concrete/Lex.lean` already uses `set_option maxRecDepth 2048` (line 13) and `set_option maxRecDepth 100000` (line 402), which `scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh:46` bans (`\bset_option\b`) and [Concrete/README.md:505](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L505) (Gate 2) bans across `Concrete/`. Needing `maxRecDepth 100000` to run `by decide` on 9-byte examples also shows that the `Decidable` instances in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:88-110` will blow the kernel reducer stack on real slice-0 certificate checks (`cert_denotes ... := by decide`, [Concrete/README.md:451-452](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L451-L452)). - **Long-term fix**:   Extend `trust_ban.sh` (or `slice0_trusted_base.sh`) to enforce the trust ban over `Concrete/`, register `Concrete.Lex`'s soundness and completeness theorems in `Concrete/Premises.lean` and `tests/golden/slice0_trusted_base.txt`, and eliminate both `set_option maxRecDepth` directives by proving `Decidable` through boolean reflection (`iff` to a tail-recursive boolean checker) rather than deep dependent `dite` chains. #### 5. [MEDIUM] Redundant hypothesis in `checkSource_complete`, missing iff/negative-completeness forms, and unnecessary list allocation in `LineComment` - **Locations**:   - [Concrete/Lex.lean:319-330](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concret
e2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L319-L330) (`checkSource_complete`)   - [Concrete/Lex.lean:384-398](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L384-L398) (`lineComment_sound`, `lineComment_complete`)   - [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:78-80](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L78-L80) (`LineComment`) - **Problem**:   1. `checkSource_complete` requires both `(hd : Utf8.Decodes bs cs)` and `(hs : SourceOk bs)`, even though `SourceOk bs` is `∃ cs, Utf8.Decodes bs cs ∧ ∀ c ∈ cs, c ≠ 0 ∧ c ≠ 0xFEFF`.   2. Neither `decode` nor `lineComment` exposes the packaged bidirectional equivalence (`decode bs = .ok cs ↔ Utf8.Decodes bs cs`, `lineComment cs = some out ↔ LineComment cs out`) or the negative soundness lemma (`decode bs = .error e → ∀ cs, ¬ Utf8.Decodes bs cs`).   3. `LineComment` constructs `47 :: 47 :: body` even though comments are trivia discarded by the lexer ([Concrete/README.md:214](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L214)), forcing `scanLine` to allocate a copy of every comment character. - **Long-term fix**:   State and prove the clean bidirectional `↔` theorems (`decode_ok_iff`, `lineComment_some_iff`) and error-refusal lemmas (`decode_error_not_decodes`), and model comment skipping in `Surface0` as consuming comment trivia to the remaining suffix `rest` (or span length) without allocating a discarded `47 :: 47 :: body` list. #### 6. [LOW] `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` omits the `PROPOSED` module-header convention and decision-row citations - **Locations**:   - [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:1-8](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L1-L8) - **Problem**:   Every other module in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/` carries the `PROPOSED: not normative until the owner freezes Core (ROADMAP A2c). Part of ConcreteSpec.Spec; see ConcreteSpec/README.md.` header, and `ROADMAP.md:331` / `docs/proposals/SPEC_UNIFICATION.md:758-759` require each spec rule's doc comment to cite the `docs/decisions.md` row it encodes (`SYN-5@3`, `SYN-6@3`). `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` omits both. - **Long-term fix**:   Add the standard `PROPOSED` header to `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` and cite the governing decision rows in each declaration's doc comment. REPOSITORY: readable VERDICT: REJECT
unbalan+ 2889817 2889815 2889817  0   50 15:26 ?        00:00:00 /home/unbalancedparen/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-linux-x64/vendor/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/bin/codex exec -s danger-full-access You are the writer for branch wip/slice0-lexer of the Concrete repo, in this clone (~/projects/clones/wip-slice0-lexer-w1r), head 7e8c926c0 (you wrote it: the slice-0 lexer foundation, ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean and Concrete/Lex.lean). A full-access agy review REJECTED it; a Kimi review ACCEPTED it with one low finding (the compiler-side lexer proofs are outside the axiom inventories). agy's findings are quoted at the end. The coordinator ruled on each. Fix all of them in new commits on wip/slice0-lexer (do not amend, do not push).  1. NOT an owner question: it is decided, a citation gap. Item 30 of the owner-approved language list (being recorded on wip/record-language-r at docs/decisions.md:1265): "Source text (OPEN-1): UTF-8 source. Whitespace is space, tab, LF and CR. A `//` comment ends at LF, CR or end of file. There are no block comments, BOM, shebang or NUL." So bare CR ending a comment and refusing NUL/BOM in source are decided. Cite item 30 in the doc comments. State explicitly that Core Q4.2 ("UTF-8 including embedded NUL") concerns static text VALUES (a string's contents may hold NUL through the `\0` escape), not raw source bytes. Refusing U+FEFF anywhere (not only at offset 0) follows from "no BOM" plus the owner's no-hidden-surprises rule: cite both. 2. One authoritative UTF-8 definition: reuse ConcreteSpec.Borrow's UTF-8/scalar definitions (or move the single definition to one shared spec module both import) instead of the second Surface0.Utf8; prove any bridging lemmas once. Move the specification-level theorems (encodes_scalar, decodes_unique, encodes_step_unique, encodes_determ, lineComment_unique and helpers) into ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Surface0.lean (imported by ConcreteSpec.lean), so the spec proof gates (axiom