Line` ([Concrete/Lex.lean:348-351](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L348-L351)) is non-tail-recursive.   3. `badSequence` ([Concrete/Lex.lean:43](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L43)) labels a non-continuation byte (`b < 0x80 ∨ b > 0xBF`, such as ASCII `0x41` after `0xC2` in [Concrete/Lex.lean:412](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L412)) as `.unexpectedContinuation` even when `b` is not a continuation byte.   4. No theorem connects `.error e` to the specification; the first-error-offset theorem was deferred as a TODO in `changelog.d/2026-11-08-lexer-utf8.md:5-6`. Under the 2026-11-08 owner rule (never cut corners; implement the best long-term design), shipping an unproved `badSequence` sidecar and deferring the error theorem is a shortcut. - **Long-term fix**:   Factor single-scalar decoding into one total step function `decodeStep (off : Nat) (bs : List UInt8) : Except DecodeError (Nat × Nat × List UInt8)` that dispatches on the lead byte's length class and fails immediately at the first offending byte, iterate it tail-recursively so execution short-circuits on the first error in $O(1)$ stack space, distinguish a missing continuation byte from a lone continuation byte, and prove the first-error-offset soundness theorem now rather than leaving a TODO. #### 4. [HIGH] `Concrete/Lex.lean` is completely outside the proof-integrity and trusted-base gates, and relies on `set_option maxRecDepth` - **Locations**:   - [Concrete/Lex.lean:13](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L13) (`set_option maxRecDepth 2048`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:402](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L402) (`set_option maxRecDepth 100000`)   - [Concrete/Premises.lean:64-72](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Premises.lean#L64-L72)   - [tests/golden/slice0_trusted_base.txt:10-16](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/tests/golden/slice0_trusted_base.txt#L10-L16)   - [scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh:42-50](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh#L42-L50) - **Problem**:   1. `scripts/proofs/*` checks only `ConcreteSpec`, and `scripts/checks/compiler/slice0_trusted_base.sh` checks only the theorem names listed in `Concrete.Premises.theorems` ([Concrete/Premises.lean:64-72](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Premises.lean#L64-L72)). Because `Concrete.Lex`'s theorems are not registered in `Concrete.Premises.theorems` and `trust_ban.sh` does not scan `Concrete/`, a `sorry`, `native_decide`, or extra axiom in `Concrete/Lex.lean` would pass every gate.   2. `Concrete/Lex.lean` already uses `set_option maxRecDepth 2048` (line 13) and `set_option maxRecDepth 100000` (line 402), which `scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh:46` bans (`\bset_option\b`) and [Concrete/README.md:505](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L505) (Gate 2) bans across `Concrete/`. Needing `maxRecDepth 100000` to run `by decide` on 9-byte examples also shows that the `Decidable` instances in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:88-110` will blow the kernel reducer stack on real slice-0 certificate checks (`cer
