ncedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L122-L123)   - [Concrete/Lex.lean:18-26](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L18-L26), [Concrete/Lex.lean:182-187](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L182-L187), [Concrete/Lex.lean:345-351](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L345-L351), [Concrete/Lex.lean:424-429](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L424-L429), [Concrete/Lex.lean:435](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L435) - **Problem**:   1. `SourceOk` (`∃ cs, Utf8.Decodes bs cs ∧ ∀ c ∈ cs, c ≠ 0 ∧ c ≠ 0xFEFF`) encodes a source-wide ban on `U+0000` and `U+FEFF` at every position in the file prior to lexing, and classifies any `U+FEFF` anywhere in the file (even at byte offset `> 0`, e.g. [Concrete/Lex.lean:427](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L427)) as `.bom`. `SYN-5@3` ([docs/decisions.md:1076-1078](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/docs/decisions.md#L1076-L1078)) states only that *"A source file is UTF-8 text"*; no owner decision establishes a pre-lexing `U+0000`/`U+FEFF` filter over the whole file (which would also ban `U+FEFF` inside comments and string literals).   2. `LineEnd c := c = 10 ∨ c = 13` makes bare `CR` (`13`) end a `//` line comment. Neither `SYN-6@3` nor any owner decision approves bare `CR` as a line terminator; the frozen compiler ended `//` comments only at `LF` (`10`) or EOF ([legacy/Concrete/Frontend/Lexer.lean:90-95](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/legacy/Concrete/Frontend/Lexer.lean#L90-L95)). Allowing bare `CR` to terminate a `//` comment lets code hidden after `\r` on the same `\n`-delimited line execute. - **Long-term fix**:   Remove undecided character/line-ending rules from `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` and `Concrete/Lex.lean`. If a specific policy on leading UTF-8 BOM, control characters (`NUL`, bare `CR`), and line endings is desired for `Surface0`, present the options and a recommendation (e.g., `LF` / `CRLF` line endings only, refusing bare `CR` outside string escapes, and handling non-token characters in the token grammar) to the owner first and record the owner's dated answer in `docs/decisions.md` before encoding it in `ConcreteSpec`. #### 2. [HIGH] Duplicate UTF-8 specification in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/` and specification theorems placed in the compiler (`Concrete/Lex.lean`) instead of `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/` - **Locations**:   - [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:11-53](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L11-L53) vs. [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Borrow.lean:513-539](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Borrow.lean#L513-L539)   - [Concrete/Lex.lean:105-120](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L105-L120) (`encodes_scalar`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:168-180](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101