-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L168-L180) (`decodes_unique`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:377-382](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L377-L382) (`lineComment_unique`)   - [ConcreteSpec.lean:1-7](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec.lean#L1-L7) - **Problem**:   1. `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Borrow.lean` already defines UTF-8 scalar well-formedness (`ConcreteSpec.Borrow.isScalar`, `ConcreteSpec.Borrow.Utf8`), with `utf8_split` and `text_view_utf8` proved in `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Borrow.lean`. `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` introduces a second, unconnected UTF-8 definition (`ConcreteSpec.Surface0.Utf8`), violating P2 ("one authoritative definition") and R-0560/R-0571.   2. Pure specification theorems about `ConcreteSpec.Surface0` (`encodes_scalar`, `decodes_unique`, `encodes_step_unique`, `encodes_determ`, `lineComment_unique`) are placed in `Concrete/Lex.lean` instead of `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Surface0.lean` (cf. [Concrete/README.md:161](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L161)). As a result, `scripts/spec/lean_site.sh` displays `0` theorems for `Surface0` in the owner view, and none of the four proof-integrity gates (`axioms.sh`, `trust_ban.sh`, `kernel_replay.sh`, `external.sh`) check these theorems. - **Long-term fix**:   Unify the UTF-8 definition in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/` so source decoding and `Text`/`Borrow` share one authoritative UTF-8 specification, move the specification-level theorems (`encodes_scalar`, `decodes_unique`, `lineComment_unique`, and their helper lemmas) into `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Surface0.lean`, and import `ConcreteSpec.Proofs.Surface0` in `ConcreteSpec.lean` (updating `scripts/proofs/axioms.golden` accordingly