ent_some_iff`) and error-refusal lemmas (`decode_error_not_decodes`), and model comment skipping in `Surface0` as consuming comment trivia to the remaining suffix `rest` (or span length) without allocating a discarded `47 :: 47 :: body` list. #### 6. [LOW] `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` omits the `PROPOSED` module-header convention and decision-row citations - **Locations**:   - [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:1-8](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L1-L8) - **Problem**:   Every other module in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/` carries the `PROPOSED: not normative until the owner freezes Core (ROADMAP A2c). Part of ConcreteSpec.Spec; see ConcreteSpec/README.md.` header, and `ROADMAP.md:331` / `docs/proposals/SPEC_UNIFICATION.md:758-759` require each spec rule's doc comment to cite the `docs/decisions.md` row it encodes (`SYN-5@3`, `SYN-6@3`). `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` omits both. - **Long-term fix**:   Add the standard `PROPOSED` header to `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` and cite the governing decision rows in each declaration's doc comment. REPOSITORY: readable VERDICT: REJECT
