b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L384-L398) (`lineComment_sound`, `lineComment_complete`)   - [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:78-80](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L78-L80) (`LineComment`) - **Problem**:   1. `checkSource_complete` requires both `(hd : Utf8.Decodes bs cs)` and `(hs : SourceOk bs)`, even though `SourceOk bs` is `∃ cs, Utf8.Decodes bs cs ∧ ∀ c ∈ cs, c ≠ 0 ∧ c ≠ 0xFEFF`.   2. Neither `decode` nor `lineComment` exposes the packaged bidirectional equivalence (`decode bs = .ok cs ↔ Utf8.Decodes bs cs`, `lineComment cs = some out ↔ LineComment cs out`) or the negative soundness lemma (`decode bs = .error e → ∀ cs, ¬ Utf8.Decodes bs cs`).   3. `LineComment` constructs `47 :: 47 :: body` even though comments are trivia discarded by the lexer ([Concrete/README.md:214](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L214)), forcing `scanLine` to allocate a copy of every comment character. - **Long-term fix**:   State and prove the clean bidirectional `↔` theorems (`decode_ok_iff`, `lineComment_some_iff`) and error-refusal lemmas (`decode_error_not_decodes`), and model comment skipping in `Surface0` as consuming comment trivia to the remaining suffix `rest` (or span length) without allocating a discarded `47 :: 47 :: body` list. #### 6. [LOW] `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` omits the `PROPOSED` module-header convention and decision-row citations - **Locations**:   - [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:1-8](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L1-L8) - **Problem**:   Every other module in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/` carries the `PROPOSED: not normative until the owner freezes Core (ROADMAP A2c). Part of ConcreteSpec.Spec; see ConcreteSpec/README.md.` header, and `ROADMAP.md:331` / `docs/proposals/SPEC_UNIFICATION.md:758-759` require each spec rule's doc comment to cite the `docs/decisions.md` row it encodes (`SYN-5@3`, `SYN-6@3`). `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` omits both. - **Long-term fix**:   Add the standard `PROPOSED` header to `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` and cite the governing decision rows in each declaration's doc comment. REPOSITORY: readable VERDICT: REJECT
unbalan+ 2889817 2889815 2889956  0   50 15:26 ?        00:00:00 /home/unbalancedparen/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-linux-x64/vendor/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/bin/codex exec -s danger-full-access You are the writer for branch wip/slice0-lexer of the Concrete repo, in this clone (~/projects/clones/wip-slice0-lexer-w1r), head 7e8c926c0 (you wrote it: the slice-0 lexer foundation, ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean and Concrete/Lex.lean). A full-access agy review REJECTED it; a Kimi review ACCEPTED it with one low finding (the compiler-side lexer proofs are outside the axiom inventories). agy's findings are quoted at the end. The coordinator ruled on each. Fix all of them in new commits on wip/slice0-lexer (do not amend, do not push).  1. NOT an owner question: it is decided, a citation gap. Item 30 of the owner-approved language list (being recorded on wip/record-language-r at docs/decisions.md:1265): "Source text (OPEN-1): UTF-8 source. Whitespace is space, tab, LF and CR. A `//` comment ends at LF, CR or end of file. There are no block comments, BOM, shebang or NUL." So bare CR ending a comment and refusing NUL/BOM in source are decided. Cite item 30 in the doc comments. State explicitly that Core Q4.2 ("UTF-8 including embedded NUL") concerns static text VALUES (a string's contents may hold NUL through the `\0` escape), not raw source bytes. Refusing U+FEFF anywhere (not only at offset 0) follows from "no BOM" plus the owner's no-hidden-surprises rule: cite both. 2. One authoritative UTF-8 definition: reuse ConcreteSpec.Borrow's UTF-8/scalar definitions (or move the single definition to one shared spec module both import) instead of the second Surface0.Utf8; prove any bridging lemmas once. Move the specification-level theorems (encodes_scalar, decodes_unique, encodes_step_unique, encodes_determ, lineComment_unique and helpers) into ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Surface0.lean (imported by ConcreteSpec.lean), so the spec proof gates (axioms.sh, trust_ban.sh, kernel_replay.sh, external.sh) cover them; keep implementation-correspondence theorems with the implementation. 3. Errors: prove the error results, including the first-error offset (the offset is the first byte at which no well-formed continuation exists — state it declaratively and prove the decoder returns exactly it), fix the mislabelled error (a non-continuation byte where a continuation is required is not `.unexpectedContinuation`; distinguish a missing/invalid continuation from a lone continuation byte), and stop at the first error: factor one total single-scalar step, iterate it so decoding and the NUL/BOM source check short-circuit at the first error (no whole-file evaluation before reporting), structurally recursive or tail-recursive. 4. Trust gates: bring Concrete/ under scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh (no exemption for Lex.lean or anything else), register Concrete.Lex's soundness/completeness/error theorems in Concrete/Premises.lean and tests/golden/slice0_trusted_base.txt (and the axiom golden as the gates require). Remove both `set_option maxRecDepth` options by restructuring the proofs so they do not need them (e.g. decidable instances via a boolean checker with an iff lemma, or lemmas that scale with input length) — proof structure that scales is the point; do not add a trust_ban exemption. 5. agy's medium items: drop the redundant hypothesis in checkSource_complete, add the packaged iff forms (decode_ok_iff, lineComment_some_iff) and the negative lemma (decode error -> no decoding), and model comment skipping without building a discarded list. 6. Surface0's module header gets the standard PROPOSED header used by every ConcreteSpec/Spec module, and each declaration's doc comment cites the decision row it encodes.  OWNER RULE (2026-11-08, verbatim: "ALWAYS tell the reviewrs to do the best long term thing rather than cuitting corners"): judge and fix by the best long-term design. Never cut corners for speed, a smaller diff or fewer round