unbalan+ 2889817 2889815 2889957  0   50 15:26 ?        00:00:00 /home/unbalancedparen/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-linux-x64/vendor/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/bin/codex exec -s danger-full-access You are the writer for branch wip/slice0-lexer of the Concrete repo, in this clone (~/projects/clones/wip-slice0-lexer-w1r), head 7e8c926c0 (you wrote it: the slice-0 lexer foundation, ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean and Concrete/Lex.lean). A full-access agy review REJECTED it; a Kimi review ACCEPTED it with one low finding (the compiler-side lexer proofs are outside the axiom inventories). agy's findings are quoted at the end. The coordinator ruled on each. Fix all of them in new commits on wip/slice0-lexer (do not amend, do not push).  1. NOT an owner question: it is decided, a citation gap. Item 30 of the owner-approved language list (being recorded on wip/record-language-r at docs/decisions.md:1265): "Source text (OPEN-1): UTF-8 source. Whitespace is space, tab, LF and CR. A `//` comment ends at LF, CR or end of file. There are no block comments, BOM, shebang or NUL." So bare CR ending a comment and refusing NUL/BOM in source are decided. Cite item 30 in the doc comments. State explicitly that Core Q4.2 ("UTF-8 including embedded NUL") concerns static text VALUES (a string's contents may hold NUL through the `\0` escape), not raw source bytes. Refusing U+FEFF anywhere (not only at offset 0) follows from "no BOM" plus the owner's no-hidden-surprises rule: cite both. 2. One authoritative UTF-8 definition: reuse ConcreteSpec.Borrow's UTF-8/scalar definitions (or move the single definition to one shared spec module both import) instead of the second Surface0.Utf8; prove any bridging lemmas once. Move the specification-level theorems (encodes_scalar, decodes_unique, encodes_step_unique, encodes_determ, lineComment_unique and helpers) into ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Surface0.lean (imported by ConcreteSpec.lean), so the spec proof gates (axiom