recursive boolean checker) rather than deep dependent `dite` chains. #### 5. [MEDIUM] Redundant hypothesis in `checkSource_complete`, missing iff/negative-completeness forms, and unnecessary list allocation in `LineComment` - **Locations**:   - [Concrete/Lex.lean:319-330](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L319-L330) (`checkSource_complete`)   - [Concrete/Lex.lean:384-398](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L384-L398) (`lineComment_sound`, `lineComment_complete`)   - [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:78-80](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L78-L80) (`LineComment`) - **Problem**:   1. `checkSource_complete` requires both `(hd : Utf8.Decodes bs cs)` and `(hs : SourceOk bs)`, even though `SourceOk bs` is `∃ cs, Utf8.Decodes bs cs ∧ ∀ c ∈ cs, c ≠ 0 ∧ c ≠ 0xFEFF`.   2. Neither `decode` nor `lineComment` exposes the packaged bidirectional equivalence (`decode bs = .ok cs ↔ Utf8.Decodes bs cs`, `lineComment cs = some out ↔ LineComment cs out`) or the negative soundness lemma (`decode bs = .error e → ∀ cs, ¬ Utf8.Decodes bs cs`).   3. `LineComment` constructs `47 :: 47 :: body` even though comments are trivia discarded by the lexer ([Concrete/README.md:214](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L214)), forcing `scanLine` to allocate a copy of every comment character. - **Long-term fix**:   State and prove the clean bidirectional `↔` theorems (`decode_ok_iff`, `lineComment_some_iff`) and error-refusal lemmas (`decode_error_not_decodes`), and model comment skipping in `Surface0` as consuming comment trivia to the remaining 