ncedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L122-L123)   - [Concrete/Lex.lean:18-26](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L18-L26), [Concrete/Lex.lean:182-187](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L182-L187), [Concrete/Lex.lean:345-351](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L345-L351), [Concrete/Lex.lean:424-429](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L424-L429), [Concrete/Lex.lean:435](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L435) - **Problem**:   1. `SourceOk` (`∃ cs, Utf8.Decodes bs cs ∧ ∀ c ∈ cs, c ≠ 0 ∧ c ≠ 0xFEFF`) encodes a source-wide ban on `U+0000` and `U+FEFF` at every position in the file prior to lexing, and classifies any `U+FEFF` anywhere in the file (even at byte offset `> 0`, e.g. [Concrete/Lex.lean:427](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L427)) as `.bom`. `SYN-5@3` ([docs/decisions.md:1076-1078](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/docs/decisions.md#L1076-L1078)) states only that *"A source file is UTF-8 text"*; no owner decision establishes a pre-lexing `U+0000`/`U+FEFF` filter over the whole file (which would also ban `U+FEFF` inside comments and string literals).   2. `LineEnd c := c = 10 ∨ c = 13` makes bare `CR` (`13`) end a `//` line comment. Neither `SYN-6@3` nor any owner decision approves bare `CR` as a line terminator; the frozen compiler ended `//` comments only at `LF` (`10`) or EOF ([legacy/Concrete/Frontend/Lexer.lean:90-95](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/legacy/Concrete/Frontend/Lexer.lean#L90-L95)). Allowing bare `CR` to terminate a `//` comment lets code hidden after `\r` on the same `\n`-delimited line execute. - **Long-term fix**:   Remove undecided character/line-ending rules from `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` and `Concrete/Lex.lean`. If a specific policy on leading UTF-8 BOM, control characters (`NUL`, bare `CR`), and line endings is desired for `Surface0`, present the options and a recommendation (e.g., `LF` / `CRLF` line endings only, refusing bare `CR` outside string escapes, and handling non-token characters in the token grammar) to the owner first and record the owner's dated answer in `docs/decisions.md` before encoding it in `ConcreteSpec`. #### 2. [HIGH] Duplicate UTF-8 specification in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/` and specification theorems placed in the compiler (`Concrete/Lex.lean`) instead of `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/` - **Locations**:   - [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:11-53](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L11-L53) vs. [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Borrow.lean:513-539](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Borrow.lean#L513-L539)   - [Concrete/Lex.lean:105-120](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L105-L120) (`encodes_scalar`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:168-180](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L168-L180) (`decodes_unique`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:377-382](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L377-L382) (`lineComment_unique`)   - [ConcreteSpec.lean:1-7](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec.lean#L1-L7) - **Problem**:   1. `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Borrow.lean` already defines UTF-8 scalar well-formedness (`ConcreteSpec.Borrow.isScalar`, `ConcreteSpec.Borrow.Utf8`), with `utf8_split` and `text_view_utf8` proved in `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Borrow.lean`. `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` introduces a second, unconnected UTF-8 definition (`ConcreteSpec.Surface0.Utf8`), violating P2 ("one authoritative definition") and R-0560/R-0571.   2. Pure specification theorems about `ConcreteSpec.Surface0` (`encodes_scalar`, `decodes_unique`, `encodes_step_unique`, `encodes_determ`, `lineComment_unique`) are placed in `Concrete/Lex.lean` instead of `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Surface0.lean` (cf. [Concrete/README.md:161](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L161)). As a result, `scripts/spec/lean_site.sh` displays `0` theorems for `Surface0` in the owner view, and none of the four proof-integrity gates (`axioms.sh`, `trust_ban.sh`, `kernel_replay.sh`, `external.sh`) check these theorems. - **Long-term fix**:   Unify the UTF-8 definition in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/` so source decoding and `Text`/`Borrow` share one authoritative UTF-8 specification, move the specification-level theorems (`encodes_scalar`, `decodes_unique`, `lineComment_unique`, and their helper lemmas) into `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Surface0.lean`, and import `ConcreteSpec.Proofs.Surface0` in `ConcreteSpec.lean` (updating `scripts/proofs/axioms.golden` accordingly). #### 3. [HIGH] Unproved error reporting, non-short-circuiting non-tail recursion in `decodeAt`/`sourceAt`, and deferred first-error-offset TODO - **Locations**:   - [Concrete/Lex.lean:31-51](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L31-L51) (`badSequence`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:58-80](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L58-L80) (`decodeAt`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:182-212](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L182-L212) (`sourcePrepend`, `sourceAt`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:348-351](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L348-L351) (`scanLine`)   - [changelog.d/2026-11-08-lexer-utf8.md:5-6](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/changelog.d/2026-11-08-lexer-utf8.md#L5-L6) - **Problem**:   1. `sourcePrepend` ([Concrete/Lex.lean:182-187](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L182-L187)) states `/-- Refuse NUL or BOM before inspecting the remaining source. -/`, and is called as `sourcePrepend off a.toNat (sourceAt (off + 1) bs)`. Because Lean 4 is call-by-value, `sourceAt (off + 1) bs` is evaluated across the entire remainder of the file *before* `sourcePrepend` executes.   2. Both `decodeAt` and `sourceAt` duplicate the 4-way match, recurse in non-tail position (`prepend ... (decodeAt ...)`), and inspect up to 4 bytes `[a, b, c, d]` before calling `badSequence` even when `a` is a 1-, 2-, or 3-byte lead that already failed at `a` or `b`. Similarly, `scan