an:402](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L402) (`set_option maxRecDepth 100000`)   - [Concrete/Premises.lean:64-72](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Premises.lean#L64-L72)   - [tests/golden/slice0_trusted_base.txt:10-16](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/tests/golden/slice0_trusted_base.txt#L10-L16)   - [scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh:42-50](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh#L42-L50) - **Problem**:   1. `scripts/proofs/*` checks only `ConcreteSpec`, and `scripts/checks/compiler/slice0_trusted_base.sh` checks only the theorem names listed in `Concrete.Premises.theorems` ([Concrete/Premises.lean:64-72](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Premises.lean#L64-L72)). Because `Concrete.Lex`'s theorems are not registered in `Concrete.Premises.theorems` and `trust_ban.sh` does not scan `Concrete/`, a `sorry`, `native_decide`, or extra axiom in `Concrete/Lex.lean` would pass every gate.   2. `Concrete/Lex.lean` already uses `set_option maxRecDepth 2048` (line 13) and `set_option maxRecDepth 100000` (line 402), which `scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh:46` bans (`\bset_option\b`) and [Concrete/README.md:505](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L505) (Gate 2) bans across `Concrete/`. Needing `maxRecDepth 100000` to run `by decide` on 9-byte examples also shows that the `Decidable` instances in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:88-110` will blow the ke