. K1's design must supply all of it. c. One explanation page per rule ID, with a failing example and its fixed version, generated from the rule's Lean doc comment and conformance examples (no second prose source, rule 5/6). A `concrete explain <rule>` command is new CLI surface: an owner question (one way per thing). d. A message style guide: second person, no unexplained jargon, show the code, say what to do next. A hint appears only when it is certain to be correct (decided: a fix is offered only after recheck, auto-applied only if a lemma proves it meaning-preserving). e. No cascades: the owner's item 12 stops at the first error per file. Is that enough (multiple files, errors after recovery, agent workflows)? f. A quality gate: golden diagnostics (T-f) plus a model reviewer that scores every new or changed message against the style guide; a refusal without a reviewed golden fails. The lexer and parser are writing refusals now, so the format is needed before slice 1.  === KLIST.md (K1) === K1. Source provenance through every IR: every node in HIR, Core, MIR, CFG, SSA and BIR carries its origin span and a stable ID, so diagnostics, trap-site accounting, debug info and facts all work. Costly to retrofit.
